 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Specifically phosphorylates seryl-tRNA(Sec) to O-phosphoseryl-tRNA(Sec), an activated intermediate forselenocysteine biosynthesis. {ECO:0000250}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) = ADP + O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA(Sec); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:25037, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9742, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9947, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616, ChEBI:CHEBI:78533,ChEBI:CHEBI:78551, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216; EC=2.7.1.164;COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420; Evidence={ECO:0000250};PATHWAY: Aminoacyl-tRNA biosynthesis; selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec)biosynthesis; selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec) from L-seryl-tRNA(Sec)(archaeal/eukaryal route): step 1/2.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q8IV42-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q8IV42-2; Sequence=VSP_014989;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) kinase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference127791</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PSTK_HUMAN Reviewed; 348 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_118672</bp:comment>
